Add Saffron goal supervision

Idle root goals need a lightweight watchdog without changing Codex's
durable goal ownership.

Add a process-local supervisor that creates one bounded, hidden,
full-history helper for an active root goal. Hidden helpers neither
appear in user agent lists nor consume normal agent capacity, and their
privileged actions are authorized by registry identity rather than a
role name. The supervisor owns its communication with the parent, so
Codex does not also enqueue ordinary child-completion messages.

The helper can resume its parent, snooze with capped retry backoff,
compact parent context, or complete the goal. Snoozes are reserved for
future deadlines and independently changing external processes; user
questions and internal decisions wake the parent instead. Every snooze
records the external condition or scheduled boundary that justifies it.

On app-server turns that mention a goal, guide root agents to activate
durable goals and continue autonomously. Optional clarification uses a
supported, reversible assumption; indispensable authority or
information enters the blocked-goal process.

Cover hidden-helper accounting, authority checks, supervisor runtime
behavior, root guidance, and the app-server lifecycle.
